claim.claim-text:
8. The apparatus as described in claim 1 wherein said inverter switching circuit comprises a plurality of power transistors to produce said output signal. 9. The apparatus as described in claim 1 and further comprising a motor (138) comprising a load current during operation of said motor. 10. The apparatus as described in claim 1 wherein said sensor comprises a comparator so as to provide a feedback signal for control of said output signal. 11. The apparatus as described in claim 1 wherein said sensor comprises a processor operable to receive said signal corresponding to said electrical characteristic of said load. 12. The apparatus as described in claim 1 and further comprising means for avoiding transients. 13. A method comprising: providing a DC voltage signal; utilizing an inverter switching circuit (112) and said DC voltage signal to produce an output signal; outputting said output signal to a load (138); providing a sensor (116) electrically coupled with said inverter switching circuit; decoupling said sensor from said inverter so as to avoid transients produced by a switching transition of said inverter switching circuit. 14. The method as described in claim 13 wherein said decoupling said sensor from said inverter comprises decoupling said sensor immediately prior to until immediately after said switching transition of said inverter switching circuit. 15. The method as described in claim 13 and further comprising utilizing at least two switches (S5, S6) electrically coupled in series with said sensor and said inverter to decouple said sensor from said inverter. 16. The method as described in claim 13 and further comprising utilizing at least two switches (S7, S8) electrically coupled in parallel, said at least two switches electrically coupled with said sensor and said inverter switching circuit. 17. The method as described in claim 13 and further comprising: utilizing at least one switch (S9) electrically coupled with said sensor and said inverter switching circuit; 

 utilizing a first control signal to open said switch during a first switching transition of said inverter switching circuit; and utilizing a second control signal to open said switch during a second switching transition of said inverter switching circuit. 18. The method as described in claim 13 wherein said outputting said output signal to a load comprises providing a pulse width modulated output signal to said load; and further comprising providing a processor to process a signal received from said sensor. 19. The method as described in claim 13 and further comprising a step for avoiding transients. 20. A method comprising: providing a DC voltage signal; utilizing an inverter switching circuit and said DC voltage signal to produce a pulse width modulated output signal; outputting said pulse width modulated output signal to power a load; continuously monitoring an electrical characteristic of said load while said load is powered by said pulse width modulated output signal; discontinuing said monitoring of said electrical characteristic of said load so as to avoid an electrical transient associated with a transition of said pulse width modulated output signal. 21. The method as described in claim 20 wherein said continuously monitoring an electrical characteristic of said load comprises monitoring for a substantial portion of a half cycle of said pulse width modulated output signal. 22. The method as described in claim 21 and further comprising: resuming monitoring of said electrical characteristic after said transition of said pulse width modulated output signal is complete. 23. The method as described in claim 22 and further comprising: discontinuing said monitoring of said electrical characteristics of said load so as to avoid a second transition of said pulse width modulated output signal. 24. The method as described in claim 20 wherein said discontinuing said monitoring of said electrical characteristic of said load comprises discontinuing said monitoring immediately prior to a transition of a switch of said inverter switching circuit. 25. A pulse width modulated power supply, comprising: 

 an input (104) to receive a DC voltage signal during operation; a pulse width modulation control circuit (116) to generate control signals during operation; an inverter bridge circuit (112) electrically coupled with said input so as to receive said DC voltage signal during operation and controlled by said pulse width modulation control circuit so as to generate a pulse width modulated voltage signal; an output (108) to output said pulse width modulated voltage signal to a load during operation; a current sense resistor electrically coupled with said inverter bridge circuit; a processor (116) electrically coupled with said current sense resistor by a switching circuit so as to monitor a potential difference across said current sense resistor; a control circuit (116) to control said switching circuit so as to decouple said processor from said current sense resistor during an electrical transient produced by said inverter bridge circuit. 26. A method of providing a pulse width modulated power supply, said method comprising: providing an input to receive a DC voltage signal during operation; utilizing a pulse width modulated control circuit to generate control signals during operation; coupling an inverter bridge circuit to said input so as to receive said DC voltage signal during operation; controlling said inverter bridge circuit with said control signals generated by said pulse width modulated control circuit; producing a pulse width modulated voltage signal with said inverter bridge circuit; outputting said pulse width modulated voltage signal to a load during operation; electrically coupling a current sense resistor with said inverter bridge circuit; electrically coupling a processor with said current sense resistor so as to allow said processor to monitor a voltage across said current sense resistor during operation; 

 controlling said switching circuit with a control signal so as to decouple said current sense resistor from said processor during a transient produced by said inverter bridge circuit.
